{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013AB7JV55LJgTNEYAn7s3J9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/unified_log.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Logging API.  The quic library can produce three complementary\n4\t//! logs per QUIC context — a textual trace (see [`crate::textlog`]),\n5\t//! a structured binary trace (see [`crate::binlog`]), and a qlog\n6\t//! (see [`crate::qlog`]) — but most applications only enable a\n7\t//! subset.  Each backend is described by a single [`Logger`] trait\n8\t//! object that the application optionally installs on the QUIC\n9\t//! context.  Per-connection dispatch happens through the [`Log`]\n10\t//! trait (implemented on [`Connection`]); per-context dispatch\n11\t//! happens through inherent methods on [`Quic`].  Either layer\n12\t//! fans the event out to whichever backends are registered.\n13\t//!\n14\t//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every body is `todo!()`.\n15\t//!\n16\t//! Pointer-shape and translation policy notes for this module:\n17\t//!\n18\t//! * The C `picoquic_unified_logging_t` is a 16-slot vtable.  Per\n19\t//!   the Phase 1 rule \"function pointers map to traits\" we collapse\n20\t//!   the whole vtable into a single trait, [`Logger`],\n21\t//!   because every backend installs all sixteen entries together.\n22\t//!   A QUIC context will eventually hold three optional\n23\t//!   `Box<dyn Logger>` slots (`text_log_fns` / `bin_log_fns`\n24\t//!   / `qlog_fns`); that restructuring lands when `internal.h` is\n25\t//!   translated.\n26\t//! * `Quic*` / `Connection*` — every observed caller passes a non-NULL\n27\t//!   pointer and the logger callbacks may mutate internal state.\n28\t//!   Free functions keyed on `Quic*` become inherent methods on\n29\t//!   [`Quic`]; those keyed on `Connection*` become methods on the\n30\t//!   [`Log`] trait (implemented for [`Connection`]).\n31\t//! * `Path*` — non-NULL for every per-path log event except\n32\t//!   [`Logger::dropped_packet`] and\n33\t//!   [`Logger::packet`], where `packet.c` may pass NULL when\n34\t//!   the path lookup failed.  Those two get `Option<&mut Path>`; the\n35\t//!   rest get `&mut Path`.\n36\t//! * `ConnectionId*` — `dcid` in [`Logger::packet_lost`] is\n37\t//!   nullable per `loss_recovery.c` (the call site explicitly\n38\t//!   substitutes NULL when no remote CID is known); the `cid`\n39\t//!   parameter to [`Logger::quic_app_message`] is always\n40\t//!   non-NULL and read-only.  `Option<&ConnectionId>` and\n41\t//!   `&ConnectionId` respectively.\n42\t//! * `struct sockaddr*` → `&core::net::SocketAddr`, matching the\n43\t//!   convention established in [`crate`].\n44\t//! * `va_list` / variadic — collapsed to [`core::fmt::Arguments`].\n45\t//!   The C `_v` variants disappear: the `format_args!` macro at the\n46\t//!   call site is the Rust substitute for both the variadic and the\n47\t//!   `va_list` flavours.\n48\t//! * `int receiving` / `int is_local` — pure 0/1 flags, promoted to\n49\t//!   `bool`.\n50\t//! * `const uint8_t* + size_t` pairs collapse to `&[u8]`; a NULL\n51\t//!   pointer with len 0 in C maps cleanly to an empty Rust slice.\n52\t//! * `picoquic_log_dropped_packet`'s `raw_data` parameter is\n53\t//!   `UNUSED` in the C wrapper and never reaches the trait, so it is\n54\t//!   dropped from the Rust API entirely.\n55\t\n56\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n57\t\n58\tuse crate::Instant;\n59\tuse crate::internal::{PacketHeader, PacketType};\n60\tuse crate::{Connection, ConnectionId, Path, Quic};\n61\t\n62\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n63\t// Unified-logger vtable.\n64\t//\n65\t// One trait covers all sixteen function-pointer slots of\n66\t// `picoquic_unified_logging_t`.  Every concrete logger (text /\n67\t// binary / qlog) implements the full trait — the C source enforces\n68\t// \"if a logging type is documented, all three functions for that\n69\t// type shall be documented as well\" by convention; the trait\n70\t// requirement makes that explicit.\n71\t//\n72\t// Method names drop the `log_` prefix from the C function-pointer\n73\t// typedefs since the trait name already conveys \"logging\".\n74\t\n75\t/// One installable logging backend.  Each method emits one record\n76\t/// of the named kind into whatever sink the backend owns (text\n77\t/// file, binary trace, qlog).\n78\tpub trait Logger {\n79\t    /// Emit a free-form application message routed by a connection-id\n80\t    /// hint rather than a live `Connection` handle.  C:\n81\t    /// `picoquic_log_quic_app_message_fn`.\n82\t    fn quic_app_message(\n83\t        &mut self,\n84\t        quic: &mut Quic,\n85\t        cid: &ConnectionId,\n86\t        args: core::fmt::Arguments<'_>,\n87\t    );\n88\t\n89\t    /// Emit a context-level UDP-datagram arrival or departure for\n90\t    /// an unknown connection.  C: `picoquic_log_quic_pdu_fn`.\n91\t    fn quic_pdu(\n92\t        &mut self,\n93\t        quic: &mut Quic,\n94\t        receiving: bool,\n95\t        current_time: Instant,\n96\t        cid64: u64,\n97\t        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n98\t        addr_local: &SocketAddr,\n99\t        packet_length: usize,\n100\t    );\n101\t\n102\t    /// Release any QUIC-context-level resource the backend owns\n103\t    /// (file handles, qlog buffers, …).  Invoked at context\n104\t    /// teardown.  C: `picoquic_log_quic_close`.\n105\t    fn quic_close(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic);\n106\t\n107\t    /// Emit a free-form application message attached to a live\n108\t    /// connection.  C: `picoquic_log_app_message_fn` — the `va_list`\n109\t    /// flavour collapses to [`core::fmt::Arguments`].\n110\t    fn app_message(&mut self, connection: &mut Connection, args: core::fmt::Arguments<'_>);\n111\t\n112\t    /// Emit a per-connection UDP-datagram arrival or departure\n113\t    /// record.  C: `picoquic_log_pdu_fn`.\n114\t    fn pdu(\n115\t        &mut self,\n116\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n117\t        receiving: bool,\n118\t        current_time: Instant,\n119\t        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n120\t        addr_local: &SocketAddr,\n121\t        packet_length: usize,\n122\t        unique_path_id: u64,\n123\t        ecn: u8,\n124\t    );\n125\t\n126\t    /// Emit a decrypted-packet record.  `receiving == true` for\n127\t    /// arrivals.  C: `picoquic_log_packet_fn`.\n128\t    fn packet(\n129\t        &mut self,\n130\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n131\t        path_x: Option<&mut Path>,\n132\t        receiving: bool,\n133\t        current_time: Instant,\n134\t        ph: &PacketHeader,\n135\t        bytes: &[u8],\n136\t    );\n137\t\n138\t    /// Emit a record that the packet was dropped due to some error.\n139\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_dropped_packet_fn`.\n140\t    fn dropped_packet(\n141\t        &mut self,\n142\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n143\t        path_x: Option<&mut Path>,\n144\t        ph: &PacketHeader,\n145\t        packet_size: usize,\n146\t        err: i32,\n147\t        current_time: Instant,\n148\t    );\n149\t\n150\t    /// Emit a record that the packet was buffered waiting for\n151\t    /// decryption.  C: `picoquic_log_buffered_packet_fn`.\n152\t    fn buffered_packet(\n153\t        &mut self,\n154\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n155\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n156\t        ptype: PacketType,\n157\t        current_time: Instant,\n158\t    );\n159\t\n160\t    /// Emit a record that a packet was formatted, ready to be sent.\n161\t    /// `bytes` is the unencrypted form (length carried in the\n162\t    /// slice); `send_buffer` is the encrypted-and-padded wire form.\n163\t    /// `pn_length` is the length of the packet-number field within\n164\t    /// `bytes`.  C: `picoquic_log_outgoing_packet_fn`.\n165\t    fn outgoing_packet(\n166\t        &mut self,\n167\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n168\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n169\t        bytes: &[u8],\n170\t        sequence_number: u64,\n171\t        pn_length: usize,\n172\t        send_buffer: &[u8],\n173\t        current_time: Instant,\n174\t    );\n175\t\n176\t    /// Emit a packet-lost record.  `dcid` may be `None` when the\n177\t    /// remote connection ID is not known at the time of detection.\n178\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_packet_lost_fn`.\n179\t    fn packet_lost(\n180\t        &mut self,\n181\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n182\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n183\t        ptype: PacketType,\n184\t        sequence_number: u64,\n185\t        trigger: &str,\n186\t        dcid: Option<&ConnectionId>,\n187\t        packet_size: usize,\n188\t        current_time: Instant,\n189\t    );\n190\t\n191\t    /// Emit a negotiated-ALPN record.  Empty `sni` / `alpn` slices\n192\t    /// stand in for the C `(NULL, 0)` callers.  C:\n193\t    /// `picoquic_log_negotiated_alpn_fn`.\n194\t    fn negotiated_alpn(\n195\t        &mut self,\n196\t        connection: &mut Connection,\n197\t        is_local: bool,\n198\t        sni: &[u8],\n199\t        alpn: &[u8],\n200\t        alpn_list: &[&[u8]],\n201\t    );\n202\t\n203\t    /// Emit a transport-extension record formatted by the local peer\n204\t    /// (`is_local == true`) or received from the remote peer.  C:\n205\t    /// `picoquic_log_transport_extension_fn`.\n206\t    fn transport_extension(&mut self, connection: &mut Connection, is_local: bool, params: &[u8]);\n207\t\n208\t    /// Emit a TLS session-ticket record.  C:\n209\t    /// `picoquic_log_tls_ticket_fn`.\n210\t    fn tls_ticket(&mut self, connection: &mut Connection, ticket: &[u8]);\n211\t\n212\t    /// Emit a connection-start record.  C:\n213\t    /// `picoquic_log_new_connection_fn`.\n214\t    fn new_connection(&mut self, connection: &mut Connection);\n215\t\n216\t    /// Emit a connection-end record.  C:\n217\t    /// `picoquic_log_close_connection_fn`.\n218\t    fn close_connection(&mut self, connection: &mut Connection);\n219\t\n220\t    /// Emit a snapshot of congestion-control parameters for one\n221\t    /// path.  C: `picoquic_log_cc_dump_fn` — the public dispatcher\n222\t    /// [`Log::cc_dump`] iterates the connection's paths and\n223\t    /// invokes this method per-path.\n224\t    fn cc_dump(&mut self, connection: &mut Connection, path_x: &mut Path, current_time: Instant);\n225\t}\n226\t\n227\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n228\t// Public dispatch layer.\n229\t//\n230\t// Each method below fans the event out to whichever of the three\n231\t// logger slots (`text_log_fns`, `bin_log_fns`, `qlog_fns`) the QUIC\n232\t// context has installed.  Phase 1 leaves bodies as `todo!()`;\n233\t// Phase 3 fills in the dispatch.\n234\t\n235\timpl Quic {\n236\t    /// Log an application-supplied message that is not attached to a\n237\t    /// live connection.  The connection-id `cid` is used purely as a\n238\t    /// routing hint by the backends.  Callers form the formatted\n239\t    /// message at the call site with `format_args!`.\n240\t    ///\n241\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_context_free_app_message`.\n242\t    pub fn log_app_message(&mut self, _cid: &ConnectionId, _args: core::fmt::Arguments<'_>) {\n243\t        todo!()\n244\t    }\n245\t\n246\t    /// Log arrival or departure of a UDP datagram for an unknown\n247\t    /// connection.  `cid64` is the would-be connection-id rendered\n248\t    /// as a 64-bit value.\n249\t    ///\n250\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_quic_pdu`.\n251\t    pub fn log_pdu(\n252\t        &mut self,\n253\t        _receiving: bool,\n254\t        _current_time: Instant,\n255\t        _cid64: u64,\n256\t        _addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n257\t        _addr_local: &SocketAddr,\n258\t        _packet_length: usize,\n259\t    ) {\n260\t        todo!()\n261\t    }\n262\t\n263\t    /// Tear down every installed logging backend, releasing the\n264\t    /// resources each one holds (file handles, qlog buffers, …).\n265\t    /// Invoked at QUIC-context teardown.\n266\t    ///\n267\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_close_logs`.\n268\t    pub fn close_logs(&mut self) {\n269\t        todo!()\n270\t    }\n271\t}\n272\t\n273\t/// Per-connection logging dispatcher.  Bringing this trait into\n274\t/// scope opts a caller into the unified-logging surface; each\n275\t/// method fans the event out to whichever [`Logger`] backends the\n276\t/// QUIC context has installed.  The C names (`picoquic_log_*`) drop\n277\t/// their `log_` prefix here — the trait name carries the verb.\n278\tpub trait Log {\n279\t    /// Append `args` to the connection's text log.  In C this exists\n280\t    /// in two flavours (`picoquic_log_app_message` and a `_v`/\n281\t    /// `va_list` twin); Rust folds them into one entry point — the\n282\t    /// `format_args!` macro at the call site is the variadic\n283\t    /// substitute.\n284\t    ///\n285\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_app_message`.\n286\t    fn app_message(&mut self, args: core::fmt::Arguments<'_>);\n287\t\n288\t    /// Log arrival or departure of a UDP datagram on this\n289\t    /// connection.\n290\t    ///\n291\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_pdu`.\n292\t    fn pdu(\n293\t        &mut self,\n294\t        receiving: bool,\n295\t        current_time: Instant,\n296\t        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n297\t        addr_local: &SocketAddr,\n298\t        packet_length: usize,\n299\t        unique_path_id: u64,\n300\t        ecn: u8,\n301\t    );\n302\t\n303\t    /// Log a decrypted packet.  `receiving == true` for an arrival.\n304\t    /// `path_x` is `None` when the path lookup failed (C source\n305\t    /// passes NULL).\n306\t    ///\n307\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_packet`.\n308\t    fn packet(\n309\t        &mut self,\n310\t        path_x: Option<&mut Path>,\n311\t        receiving: bool,\n312\t        current_time: Instant,\n313\t        ph: &PacketHeader,\n314\t        bytes: &[u8],\n315\t    );\n316\t\n317\t    /// Report that a packet was dropped due to some error.  The C\n318\t    /// wrapper takes a `raw_data` buffer that it then ignores\n319\t    /// (`UNUSED(raw_data)`); the parameter is dropped here.\n320\t    ///\n321\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_dropped_packet`.\n322\t    fn dropped_packet(\n323\t        &mut self,\n324\t        path_x: Option<&mut Path>,\n325\t        ph: &PacketHeader,\n326\t        packet_size: usize,\n327\t        err: i32,\n328\t        current_time: Instant,\n329\t    );\n330\t\n331\t    /// Report that a packet was buffered waiting for decryption.\n332\t    ///\n333\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_buffered_packet`.\n334\t    fn buffered_packet(&mut self, path_x: &mut Path, ptype: PacketType, current_time: Instant);\n335\t\n336\t    /// Log that a packet was formatted, ready to be sent.  `bytes`\n337\t    /// is the unencrypted packet (slice length subsumes the C\n338\t    /// `length` parameter); `send_buffer` is the encrypted wire\n339\t    /// form.  `pn_length` is the length of the packet-number field\n340\t    /// within `bytes`.\n341\t    ///\n342\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_outgoing_packet`.\n343\t    fn outgoing_packet(\n344\t        &mut self,\n345\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n346\t        bytes: &[u8],\n347\t        sequence_number: u64,\n348\t        pn_length: usize,\n349\t        send_buffer: &[u8],\n350\t        current_time: Instant,\n351\t    );\n352\t\n353\t    /// Log a packet-lost event.  `dcid` is `None` when the remote\n354\t    /// connection ID is unknown.\n355\t    ///\n356\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_packet_lost`.\n357\t    fn packet_lost(\n358\t        &mut self,\n359\t        path_x: &mut Path,\n360\t        ptype: PacketType,\n361\t        sequence_number: u64,\n362\t        trigger: &str,\n363\t        dcid: Option<&ConnectionId>,\n364\t        packet_size: usize,\n365\t        current_time: Instant,\n366\t    );\n367\t\n368\t    /// Log negotiated SNI/ALPN.  Empty `sni`/`alpn` slices match the\n369\t    /// C callers that pass `(NULL, 0)`.\n370\t    ///\n371\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_negotiated_alpn`.\n372\t    fn negotiated_alpn(&mut self, is_local: bool, sni: &[u8], alpn: &[u8], alpn_list: &[&[u8]]);\n373\t\n374\t    /// Log a transport-extension blob.  `is_local == true` when the\n375\t    /// extension was formatted by the local peer; `false` when it\n376\t    /// was received.\n377\t    ///\n378\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_transport_extension`.\n379\t    fn transport_extension(&mut self, is_local: bool, params: &[u8]);\n380\t\n381\t    /// Log a TLS session ticket.\n382\t    ///\n383\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_tls_ticket`.\n384\t    fn tls_ticket(&mut self, ticket: &[u8]);\n385\t\n386\t    /// Log the start of this connection.\n387\t    ///\n388\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_new_connection`.\n389\t    fn new_connection(&mut self);\n390\t\n391\t    /// Log the end of this connection.\n392\t    ///\n393\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_close_connection`.\n394\t    fn close_connection(&mut self);\n395\t\n396\t    /// Log a snapshot of congestion-control parameters across every\n397\t    /// path on the connection.  Iterates `connection->path[…]`\n398\t    /// internally and dispatches per-path through\n399\t    /// [`Logger::cc_dump`].\n400\t    ///\n401\t    /// C: `picoquic_log_cc_dump`.\n402\t    fn cc_dump(&mut self, current_time: Instant);\n403\t}\n404\t\n405\timpl Log for Connection {\n406\t    fn app_message(&mut self, _args: core::fmt::Arguments<'_>) {\n407\t        todo!()\n408\t    }\n409\t\n410\t    fn pdu(\n411\t        &mut self,\n412\t        _receiving: bool,\n413\t        _current_time: Instant,\n414\t        _addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n415\t        _addr_local: &SocketAddr,\n416\t        _packet_length: usize,\n417\t        _unique_path_id: u64,\n418\t        _ecn: u8,\n419\t    ) {\n420\t        todo!()\n421\t    }\n422\t\n423\t    fn packet(\n424\t        &mut self,\n425\t        _path_x: Option<&mut Path>,\n426\t        _receiving: bool,\n427\t        _current_time: Instant,\n428\t        _ph: &PacketHeader,\n429\t        _bytes: &[u8],\n430\t    ) {\n431\t        todo!()\n432\t    }\n433\t\n434\t    fn dropped_packet(\n435\t        &mut self,\n436\t        _path_x: 